                            <comment id="18671008" author="JIRAUSER129848" created="Wed, 28 Jan 2026 19:58:38 +0100"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.jnj.com/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=ASaha67&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;ASaha67&quot;&gt;Saha, Ankita [JJCUS NON-J&amp;amp;J]&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Good catch here, this was a bit of an edge case. The error is that the negative measurement (i.e. -554.77) was using the positive value (554.77) to calculate Fit for GxP. Operating limits are -600, 500 and -600 &amp;lt; 554.77 &amp;lt; 500 is false. Would have been a nasty bug, nice job.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Fix deployed and assigned back.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="18666989" author="JIRAUSER182813" created="Wed, 28 Jan 2026 15:28:15 +0100"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.jnj.com/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=CSims11&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;CSims11&quot;&gt;Sims, Cody [JRDUS]&lt;/a&gt; - As discussed, Fit for GxP is showing No instead of Yes for below use case:&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;alue for Fit for GxP = &apos;YES&apos; When&#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;GxP Level = &apos;GMP&apos; and&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Calibration Due Date/Time &amp;gt; or = Date(NOW) and&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Verification Due Date/Time &amp;gt; or = Date(NOW) and&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Life Cycle State = &apos;Active&apos; and&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Status = &apos;Active&apos; and&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Actual Amt &amp;gt;= Lower Operating Limit AND Actual Amt &amp;lt;= Upper Operating Limit&#160;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


